                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41cf5fec-3142-3d5b-b6b2-45ea01043894",
                                        "entry_id": "aa995945-4345-35ac-a28a-67deeeedad88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An exclamation of disbelief or dismissal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0db85b4e-4cc8-4dd1-8ecc-51ea511dd9b5",
                                                "sense_id": "41cf5fec-3142-3d5b-b6b2-45ea01043894",
                                                "text": "“Okay, busted. But you see all them muscles, girl?” She shakes her head, laughing. “Nope. I only have eyes for my boo.” “Girl, bye. You can still look.” She giggles. “Well, I ain’t lookin’ hard, trust.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b413d36-f250-48e1-be69-f160dfe0a10a",
                                                "sense_id": "41cf5fec-3142-3d5b-b6b2-45ea01043894",
                                                "text": "Rowlings-Blake responded: \"Girl bye, if he can't take criticism from 'a joke', what's he gonna do when somebody real comes for him? #notready\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96f8278c-3c8e-4703-8521-f7cf4c60a7b4",
                                                "sense_id": "41cf5fec-3142-3d5b-b6b2-45ea01043894",
                                                "text": "Her jeans don't even got the loops for her damn belt LMFAO bye 😭"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e18e7ca-70be-4e83-99bc-714f344d7a0f",
                                                "sense_id": "41cf5fec-3142-3d5b-b6b2-45ea01043894",
                                                "text": "\"i wish to get back a couple of katycats that left my side\" bye did she really say this..its so sad i love her sm 😢😔"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00fcb1be-4761-4495-b458-d66cd5e5d2cb",
                                                "sense_id": "41cf5fec-3142-3d5b-b6b2-45ea01043894",
                                                "text": "\"I just want Johnny to leave me alone.\" Girl, bye. Control your lap dog."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bye",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                        "entry_id": "155d0b9d-552e-3291-adc4-55f69a5ab7f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Eye dialect spelling of boy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "pronunciation-spelling"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a1ce62e-2759-4b60-8d42-ce3dd0996399",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                                "text": "\"So what shall I do, now, Patric? Can you think of any plan? \"Bedad!\" said Pat , as he scratched his head , “ I'm the very bye that can.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd4b867c-2c85-45ff-a73c-cee2fbe406de",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                                "text": "'Och,' sez I, 'there's many a bye that's lonely livin' rite wid his friends an' naybors. Sure an' I'm lonesome mesilf.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8cbd191-23c9-470a-be83-15d29a3790ed",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                                "text": "There a bye has his hand toorn off, and there a bye loses his eyesight complately, and over yan a bye has his joogular vein torn wid a whistlin' boom, and forninst that is the bye who thinks his gun isn't loaded and kills his little sisther."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b36c07b5-93ca-43ea-8c44-0ef5c9f6deaf",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                                "text": "In thim days the bye who wint to work in the foundhry to learn the thrade, in goin' into the shop in the morning would meet a big, ruffneck boss wit his blue faunel shirt on and his schleeves rolled up to his ilbows, who could show him the mishtakes he made the day befoor, if he made any."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7652851-4a35-4c64-b8f9-6c4c1f471533",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                                "text": "I know a nice bye who's goin' to git two cookies fer thim worrds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc061ef0-9ed4-48f7-b6d7-446a76fbe17e",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8c75d-0ef9-315f-924d-1bd218317ed0",
                                                "text": "Hardy, weatherbeaten, intimately familiar with the winds and tides of his local shore, capable of turning his hand to many things, squeezing a hard living from the treacherous sea—a figure rendered familiar by the words “Ise the bye who builds the boat / And ise the bye that sails her / Ise the bye who catches the fish / And takes them home to Liza.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
